<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>INTRODUCTION TO HTML DOM</title>
    <style>
        .alert{
            color: rgb(81, 8, 153);
            background-color: rgb(162, 162, 247);
            padding: 1px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1 id="heading">WELCOME</h1>
    <p>HELLO</p>
    <p>READY TO LEARN ABOUT OUR SOLAR SYSTEM?</p>
    <p>The Solar System is the gravitationally bound system that includes the Sun and all the celestial objects that orbit
    it—including eight major planets, hundreds of moons, dwarf planets, asteroids, and comets.</p>
    <script>
        let div = document.createElement("div");
        div.id = "paragraph";
        div.className = "alert";
        div.innerHTML = "<p><b>Congrats! You have learned more about our solar system.</b></p>";
         document.body.append(div);
        let heading=document.getElementById("heading");
        heading.innerHTML= "&#129680";
        document.querySelector("p").innerHTML= "<strong>Good Job!</strong>";
    </script>
</body>
</html>